; Step IY to the next newer phrase record
;
; Moves IY to the next record below it on the phrase stack that is not an
; EXCEPT record (#R$789F) and leaves the old IY in IX (the swap is #R$7896).
; #R$7892 also counts the record down in B (the number of records still to
; visit); #R$7893 does not. Records are created downwards, so "newer" is a
; lower address.
;
; B Records left to visit (#R$7892 only)
; IY Current record
; O:B Decreased by one (#R$7892 only)
; O:IY The next newer record
; O:IX The old IY
@label=StepNewerCount
c$7892 DEC B         ;
; This entry point is used by the routine at #R$75F6.
@label=StepNewer
*$7893 CALL $789F    ;
; This entry point is used by the routine at #R$788C.
@label=SwapRecordPtrs
*$7896 PUSH IX       ;
 $7898 PUSH IY       ;
 $789A POP IX        ;
 $789C POP IY        ;
 $789E RET           ;
